======================================================================
PROJECT ATTRIBUTION
======================================================================

The Resilient Immutable Archive Pagination System (RIAPS) is an
architectural strategy for constructing append-only, stable archive
pagination using immutable post-ID boundaries.

RIAPS is designed to minimize cascading archive invalidation caused by
content publication and deletion in conventional newest-first pagination
systems, while enabling stable historical archive URLs, localized cache
invalidation, efficient database retrieval, and long-lived edge caching.

The original system architecture, technical documentation, architectural
descriptions, diagrams, examples, terminology, and reference
implementations contained in this repository were authored and/or
developed by Saheed Oluwatosin Tiamiyu through TISAO Technologies LLC.

TISAO Technologies LLC is the copyright holder for the original materials
identified as copyrighted by the company in this repository.

